{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514773-the-red-rose-pack-were-wasted-potential","id":1514773,"title":"The Red Rose pack were wasted potential","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-12T16:15:50-07:00","id":1514773,"title":"The Red Rose pack were wasted potential","content":"The Red Rose pack were first introduced in Sins of the Blood and can be found on pages 105-108. They are a large pack of Sabbat infernalists that would make deals with demons on behalf of their clients (who consist of both vampires and mortals) in return for a hefty payment. They promised that since the client in question isn't dealing with the demon directly they didn't need to worry about any infernal taint.<br /> <br /> Of course, this was all a lie. Regardless of dealing with demons directly or indirectly, the fact of the matter is that the client in question intentionally chose to gain power from a demon. So even though someone else decided to deal with the demon on their behalf, the fact that they accepted power from a demon, still damns their soul to hell. Something interesting about this pack is that they have created an enterprise out of this practice and have learned how to cover their tracks, so well in fact that the Sabbat Inquisition has trouble tracking them. They have also spread their business across multiple states and seem to still be growing.<br /> <br /> I genuinely feel that they could have been an enemy that would force a truce between the sects. Here you have a large group of kindred who are ruthless, clever, and crafty in equal measure. Whose actions, threaten the existence of all vampires. They are very similar to how the Baali were during the Baali Wars, but unlike the Baali they are far more subtle in their actions and seem to have a lot more success in corrupting others. This is a great setup for another war, one that could put even the Baali Wars to shame.<br /> <br /> What do you think?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T00:03:18-07:00","id":1514805,"title":"","content":"Vampires facilitating demonic pacts sounds cool but also like a trick you could only play on neonates. Openly advertising demon connections is a no-no. Perhaps the only exception is if you had it bound, but even then it's dangerous <br /> <br /> Damnation is a tricky topic. I'm of the opinion that God in the WoD is humanity's jailor, at best he keeps us safe from whatever's outside. When things are that grim, damnation of your immortal soul shouldn't be so easy. Reincarnation seems to be how things work, so such easy damnation would cause too many problems. Anything short of the caul or a pact where you have full awareness of what you're doing and you have enough willpower (6+) to be considered spiritually developed enough to make such a deal shouldn't be considered true damnation. Otherwise all demons would have armies of really edgy kids at their disposal. <br /> <br /> You can throw the word damnation around to upset whoever will believe you though. In for a Penny, in for a pound kind of tactics are good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T03:18:08-07:00","id":1514815,"title":"","content":"It'd make for an interesting chronicle, though I certainly think it shouldn't be the direction the metaplot develops in, <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(I say, as somebody who thinks the only direction metaplot should go is straight in the bin).</span> Plus even if the Sabbat and Camarilla won't play nice directly, the Setites, Ravnos and Assamites all have a bone to pick with infernalists too.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the topic of damnation as a fate within the WoD:<br /> Changeling and Mage both support reincarnation, and while the Garou aren't human souls, they also reincarnate. So let's assume that by default sapient beings are just stuck in a loop, living again and again, trapped in the World of Darkness. (Which is a damnation all on its own, tbh)<br /> <br /> Annihilationism also appears to be fact within the WoD; unless Oblivion actually simply resets your soul and chucks it back in the cycle, falling in there is the end.<br /> (I'll be honest, given the option between having to live through that hellhole again, and simply being erased, I would probably willingly jump into the Well of the Void. Therefore, Oblivion =/= Annihilation in my games, because it's more depressing that way.)<br /> <br /> For a more hellish Hell we have the Labyrinth and Harrowings. The Shadow-Eaten are consumed by their own hatred and pain, incapable of seeing the world as anything but hell. - that one though is more of a temporary damnation and a self-inflicted fate based on one's own will and perception, where one gives up and succumbs to nihilism. It still ends in annihilation.<br /> - So vampiric damnation, flavour No.1 [Annihilation]: Your soul is simply consumed by Oblivion and erased from the cycle after the final death.<br /> <br /> There's also Yomi, which may be divinely appointed, but it's still basically a little pocket dimension that only souls ascribing to a specific paradigm get kidnapped to, rather than something that affects everyone by default. The Baali and their demons seem to be connected to the Earthbound, although there are similarities with the Neverborn Malfeans, imo, so you're probably looking into an eternity as a servant of those. Hell, as in a jail of eternal torment, doesn't seem to a default fate awaiting the worst denizens of the WoD by default; but let's assume that the embrace or making a pact involves signing up for stuff that;<br /> - Vampiric damnation, flavour No.2 [Fire and Brimstone Hell]: Your soul is taken back to a Hell dimension to suffer - probably somewhere in Malfeas or the Labyrinth to be used to power something horrible.<br /> <br /> There's the Abyss that held the Fallen is just going insane of boredom in absolute nothingness for all eternity. I don't think that was a fate ever intended for a human (or former human) soul though.<br /> - But if you'd like, Vampiric damnation, flavour No.3 [Traditional Separation from God Hell]: Nothing, forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T03:55:58-07:00","id":1514820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> infernalists that would make deals with demons on behalf of their clients (who consist of both vampires and mortals) in return for a hefty payment. They promised that since the client in question isn't dealing with the demon directly they didn't need to worry about any infernal taint.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>I also think, on a reread, they may struggle to find clients because any vampires gullible to <i>believe</i> that tend to die young. You'd probably be looking at recruiting the desperate (and finding ways to make more people that desperate).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T10:52:50-07:00","id":1514861,"title":"","content":"The Infernalist element was much heavier emphasized in First Edition and early 2nd Edition. Then dialed WAYYYYY BACK.<br /> <br /> Perhaps because it gave a one-dimensional enemy to vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T11:00:08-07:00","id":1514862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514773-the-red-rose-pack-were-wasted-potential?p=1514861#post1514861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Infernalist element was much heavier emphasized in First Edition and early 2nd Edition. Then dialed WAYYYYY BACK.<br /> <br /> Perhaps because it gave a one-dimensional enemy to vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>IDK, like, they could really pull off grey infernalists if they wanted to. Make things less about damnation and more about neonates taking quick and dirty routes to power and that's terrifying to the established social order... that's like, a third of the Xanxia novels I've seen, and some of them are even good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T11:29:07-07:00","id":1514865,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27313_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27313\" data-vbnamecard=\"27313\">Hello</a> I think that it could make for a good scenario but it isn't likely that a single pack, even if its a big pack, could be such a threat as to bring the Sabbat and Camarilla together. Both sects could be coming for this pack but I don't think that this would be the merit of a truce or bridge between the two sects.<br /> <br /> Same with the Baali Wars. Without me being a scholar on the lore, I always understood the Baali Wars to have been on a larger scale than putting down a large infernalist pack, and potentially with more on stake as well. When they put down Carthage they put down a, for that time, major city of humans filled with infernalists and Baali and stuff. A whole different scale of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514773-the-red-rose-pack-were-wasted-potential?p=1514861#post1514861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Infernalist element was much heavier emphasized in First Edition and early 2nd Edition. Then dialed WAYYYYY BACK.<br /> <br /> Perhaps because it gave a one-dimensional enemy to vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a solid improvement.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T22:23:39-07:00","id":1514918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514773-the-red-rose-pack-were-wasted-potential?p=1514865#post1514865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a solid improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't as it made people confuse the Sabbat for having a point versus acknowledging everyone is awful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T23:58:24-07:00","id":1514924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514773-the-red-rose-pack-were-wasted-potential?p=1514918#post1514918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't as it made people confuse the Sabbat for having a point versus acknowledging everyone is awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, but I'll it at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T12:01:53-07:00","id":1514992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514773-the-red-rose-pack-were-wasted-potential?p=1514924#post1514924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, but I'll it at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I'm the guy who loved DEMON: THE FALLEN and wish the Nephandi were a playable option. So yes, I'm all for Sabbat infernalists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T16:17:22-07:00","id":1515191,"title":"","content":"As far as infernalism goes, don't forget that destroying souls isn't actually something most &quot;demons&quot; in wod are capable of.<br /> <br /> Fallen can't actually keep souls very long unless they master one of the most jealously kept earthbound lores in the setting(the only one know to wield this power is an Archduke)<br /> <br /> Banes can't eat a soul without first chewing through all the person's autonomy, and if they die before then the bane is out of luck. Even then, the soul isn't destroyed, the bane and the soul just fuse(which might mean eaten souls might be released to reincarnate if the bane is killed)<br /> <br /> Spectres don't actually destroy souls when they make deals, and it's ambiguous if even the mightiest neverborn actually destroys souls when they &quot;Eat&quot; a wraith given how oblivion works(heck, neverborn might just be collections of the soulless plasm that ghosts shed with their memories when they reincarnate)<br /> <br /> Yama kings are still part of the cycle of reincarnation. They may live in a stagnant part of the cycle that makes escaping them within the next few kalpas infinitesimally unlikely, but it's a big theme that eventually the bill will come due on them as well(demon lords in book of madness seem to function similarly).<br /> <br /> The only demon type that calls this into question as a group are the uncategorized demons that make more generic infernal investment based on a 1-10 tiered pact system. Nothing is really known about these and no one knows what happens to the souls they claim.<br /> <br /> So in total, we have 1 demon that can actually eat souls, a group of unknowns that may or may not bring souls out of the reincarnation cycle, and everyone else is LARPing eternal punishment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514773-the-red-rose-pack-were-wasted-potential?p=1514815#post1514815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Annihilationism also appears to be fact within the WoD; unless Oblivion actually simply resets your soul and chucks it back in the cycle, falling in there is the end.<br /> (I'll be honest, given the option between having to live through that hellhole again, and simply being erased, I would probably willingly jump into the Well of the Void. Therefore, Oblivion =/= Annihilation in my games, because it's more depressing that way.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that we get examples in wraith of people who, full stop, fell into oblivion and are now in mortal human bodies(most famously charon himself), this is likely as close to &quot;Canon&quot; as WoD can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T04:05:41-07:00","id":1515226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514773-the-red-rose-pack-were-wasted-potential?p=1515191#post1515191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in total, we have 1 demon that can actually eat souls, a group of unknowns that may or may not bring souls out of the reincarnation cycle, and everyone else is LARPing eternal punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>And <b>the Eater of Words</b>\u200b<br /> According to the Malkavians, the Word-Eater is said to be a great, enlightened sage who went mad from the curse of Malkav, he is one of Malkav's first Children<br /> In his insane/illuminated state, he realizes that he did not have to subsist on blood, but could consume anything, become more of what he ate. The Word-Eater ate rock, sky, colors and ideas before he decided he liked ideas most of all. He began to consume words, believing it would make him wise again, and restore his sanity. So, the Word-Eater sustains himself not with blood, but with True Names - he literally of biting chunks of reality itself free from the world and gulping them down<br /> Some Malkavians say that the words he eats are gone forever - and so are the ideas. No one will never know what ideas are missing, because they are gone forever, and gone retroactively, so the Word-Eater is limiting the world to a smaller and more feeble reality all the time.<br /> <br /> Assuming he is real and indeed capable of devouring someone or something True Name? Then that soul is snuffed out like it never existed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T07:02:50-07:00","id":1515238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514773-the-red-rose-pack-were-wasted-potential?p=1515226#post1515226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And <b>the Eater of Words</b>\u200b<br /> According to the Malkavians, the Word-Eater is said to be a great, enlightened sage who went mad from the curse of Malkav, he is one of Malkav's first Children<br /> In his insane/illuminated state, he realizes that he did not have to subsist on blood, but could consume anything, become more of what he ate. The Word-Eater ate rock, sky, colors and ideas before he decided he liked ideas most of all. He began to consume words, believing it would make him wise again, and restore his sanity. So, the Word-Eater sustains himself not with blood, but with True Names - he literally of biting chunks of reality itself free from the world and gulping them down<br /> Some Malkavians say that the words he eats are gone forever - and so are the ideas. No one will never know what ideas are missing, because they are gone forever, and gone retroactively, so the Word-Eater is limiting the world to a smaller and more feeble reality all the time.<br /> <br /> Assuming he is real and indeed capable of devouring someone or something True Name? Then that soul is snuffed out like it never existed...</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make him more powerful than all the antediluvians, including his own sire, and Caine himself. Hell, I think that would make him more powerful than any mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"